## Phase 27 Important AI API Key and Security Requirement:

The platform will include AI tools, but AI must not work unless the Owner/Teacher configures an AI provider and API key.

Do not hardcode any AI API key.
Do not expose AI API keys in frontend code.
Do not store secrets in normal client-side settings.

Create an Owner AI Settings page:

/owner/settings/ai

Owner can:
- Enable/disable AI features
- Select AI provider: OpenAI / Anthropic Claude / Gemini / Other
- Add or update API key securely
- Add model name
- Set regenerate limits
- Set monthly usage limit if practical
- Test AI connection
- View masked API key only, never full key
- View AI status: configured / not configured / connection failed

Security rules:
- API key must be stored securely using environment variables or encrypted server-side storage.
- Never send the API key to the browser.
- AI requests must be made server-side only.
- If no API key is configured, AI buttons should be disabled.
- Show clear message: “AI is not configured yet. Please add your API key in Owner Settings.”
- AI usage must be logged.
- Save prompt, response, tool name, related entity, estimated tokens/cost if possible.
- AI output must be preview/draft only.
- Never auto-publish AI output.

Also create:
/owner/ai/logs

AI logs should show:
- tool name
- provider
- model
- related student/article/homework if any
- created date
- estimated tokens/cost if available
- status: success / failed
- error message if failed

Do not continue using AI tools if the key is missing or invalid.

