HTML material rules:
- HTML files can be useful for interactive lessons.
- Do not execute unsafe scripts directly inside the main app.
- Prefer sandboxed iframe for HTML preview.
- If sandboxing is not safe or not supported, show as downloadable file only.
- Prevent uploaded HTML from accessing app cookies/session.
- Never allow uploaded HTML to run with full app privileges.

Upload security:
- Validate file type and MIME.
- Validate file size using upload settings.
- Do not allow executable uploads.
- Block dangerous extensions:
  .php, .exe, .bat, .cmd, .sh, .js unless explicitly handled safely, .msi, .dll
- Store original filename, saved filename, MIME type, file size, uploader, created date.
- Protect private materials from unauthorized users.
- Student can only access assigned materials.
- Parent can only access linked child materials.

